# Cloudflare redirect rules, served ahead of the static assets.
#
# Retired content URLs go here rather than in astro.config.mjs `redirects`:
# Astro emits each config redirect as `<path>/index.html`, so registering both
# the with-slash and without-slash form of one path is a route collision, and
# both forms need to work. The Cloudflare adapter appends its own entries to
# this file at build time, so nothing here is lost.
#
# Only for URLs that were live and crawlable. A path that never shipped should
# 404, not redirect.

